('correspond','/ˌkoɹəˈspɑnd/','common',4.89,'plain','["verb"]','To be equivalent or similar in character, quantity, quality, origin, structure, function etc.','verb','From Middle French correspondre, from Latin com- (“with”) + respondeo (“to match, to answer to”), equivalent to co- + respond.',126,'120_200',1,0.75,55),
('rudraksha',NULL,'scarce',1.5,'plain','["noun"]','The dried seed of a large evergreen broad-leaved tree, Elaeocarpus ganitrus, which is traditionally used as prayer beads in Hinduism.','noun','From Sanskrit रुद्राक्ष (rudrākṣa, “Rudra''s eyes”), from रुद्र (Rudra, “Rudra, a Rigvedic deity of wind and storm”), and अक्ष (ákṣa, “eye”), variant form of अक्षि (ákṣi).',170,'120_200',1,0.65,56),
