('North West River','/ˈnɔɹθ ˈwɛst ˈɹɪv.əɹ/','rare',NULL,'multiword,capitalized','["proper noun"]','A town in Labrador, Newfoundland and Labrador.','proper noun','The settlement is named for its location near Little Lake, which appears to be a north-western river when viewed from Lake Melville.',132,'120_200',0,0.6,258),
('scalar','/skeɪ.lɚ/','common',3.66,'plain','["noun", "adjective"]','A quantity that has magnitude but not direction.','noun','Borrowed from Latin scālāris, adjectival form from scāla (“a flight of steps, stairs, staircase, ladder, scale”), for *scadla, from scandere (“to climb”); compare scale. The mathematics sense was coined by Irish mathematician and astronomer William Rowan Hamilton in 1846.',272,'200plus',1,0.8,259),
