('Veles',NULL,'scarce',1.61,'capitalized','["proper noun"]','The pagan Slavic god of the fertile earth, livestock, waters, and the underworld, often portrayed as a chimera.','proper noun','Likely of Proto-Indo-European origin but the exact root is difficult to pinpoint. Suggestions have included *h₂welh₁- (“wool”) and *welg- (“damp, humid”). Also compare Lithuanian vẽlės (“ghostly figures of the deceased”), archaic form of modern velnias (“demon, devil”). More at Veles.',285,'200plus',1,0.75,321),
