('diptych','/ˈdɪptɪk/','uncommon',2.27,'plain','["noun"]','A writing tablet consisting of two leaves of rigid material connected by hinges and shutting together so as to protect the writing within.','noun','From Late Latin diptycha, plural, from Ancient Greek, neuter plural of δίπτυχος (díptukhos, “folded, doubled”), from δι- (di-) + πτυχή (ptukhḗ, “fold, layer”).',159,'120_200',1,0.75,327),
