('Haar space',NULL,'unattested',NULL,'multiword,capitalized','["noun"]','A finite-dimensional subspace V of 𝒞(X, 𝕂), where X is a compact space and 𝕂 either the real numbers or the complex numbers, such that for any given f∈𝒞(X, 𝕂) there is exactly one element of V that approximates f "best", i.e. with minimum distance to f in supremum norm.','noun','Named after Hungarian mathematician Alfréd Haar.',48,'40_80',1,0.44,480),
