('Thessaloniki','/ˌθɛsələˈniːki/','uncommon',2.63,'capitalized','["proper noun"]','A port city, the capital of Central Macedonia, in northern Greece.','proper noun','From Greek Θεσσαλονίκη (Thessaloníki), from Ancient Greek Θεσσαλονίκη (Thessaloníkē), named for Thessalonike daughter of Philip II, half-sister of Alexander the Great, and wife of Cassander of Macedonia, from Θεσσᾰλός (Thessălós, “Thessalian”) + νῑ́κη (nī́kē, “victory”), possibly named for her birth on the anniversary of the Battle of Crocus Field.',350,'200plus',1,0.8,495),
